  :adr/scope-confirmed-by-owner-mi-sec "owner explicitly confirmed, via AskUserQuestion before implementation: full SEC EDGAR universe (8000+ filers, not a curated pilot list) and auto-merge (server-side merge API) for periodic ingestion output, not PR-only manual review"
  :adr/schema-extension-mi-sec "new :company/* attribute family in data/schema.edn (cik/name/ticker/sic/isic/isic-confidence/revenue-usd/assets-usd/net-income-usd/shares-outstanding/fiscal-period/as-of/confidence/source/source-url/fetch-etag), same flat-EAV-no-ref discipline as pre-existing :market/*. New optional :market/isic attribute backfilled onto 5 of the 14 existing 2022 facts where the ISIC correspondence was unambiguous; left unset elsewhere rather than force a bad mapping."
  :adr/real-bugs-found-mi-sec "5 real parsing bugs found only by hitting the live SEC EDGAR API, not from documentation: (1) stale-tag bug -- naive first-match tag selection would report Apple's frozen pre-ASC-606 us-gaap:Revenues tag as current; fixed to pick by most-recent date across all present tags. (2) anchor-date bug -- dei:EntityCommonStockSharesOutstanding's cover-page date can postdate the shared fiscal-year-end of revenue/assets/net-income; :company/as-of now anchors only to financial-statement concepts. (3) roster-ordering bug -- company_tickers.json's numeric-string-keyed JSON parses to a Clojure PersistentHashMap with hash-order iteration, not file order; fixed by sorting on the numeric index (verified: keys returned as (:0 :4 :1 :2 :3)). (4) conditional-GET reality -- data.sec.gov's companyfacts/submissions endpoints never honor If-Modified-Since/ETag (always 200, verified by double-fetching the same CIK); only company_tickers.json (different host) actually returns 304 (also verified). (5) CIK type inconsistency -- companyfacts' top-level cik is a bare int, submissions' is already zero-padded string; :company/cik is now always taken from the caller's canonical value, never either endpoint's self-reported field."
  :adr/no-market-cap-mi-sec "R0 deliberately does NOT carry :company/market-cap-usd -- XBRL companyfacts has no share price, and market cap requires a price feed. Honest fundamentals-only scope (revenue/assets/net-income/shares-outstanding), all :measured. A future bridge to cloud-itonami-isic-6311's licensed price feeds (mirroring kotoba.securities.pricing's existing bridge pattern) is an explicit follow-up, not attempted here."
  :adr/grounding-gate-extension-analyst-sec "new src/analyst/citation.cljc resolve-citation tries market-intel.store/category then company-of for every cited id (never type-guessing which store to hit -- both tried, so a future id-shape change fails loud, not silent). policy.cljc's grounding/confidence-transparency/staleness checks and advisor.cljc's 4 mi/category call sites (compare/rank/report/llm-advisor) now route through this shared resolver uniformly. No new analysis operation type was added -- existing :market/compare :market/rank :market/report handle mixed market+company citations as-is."
  :adr/live-verification-mi-sec "28 real companies (SEC EDGAR live data) ingested into data/company-facts.edn and verified across LangchainDbStore/DataScriptStore parity, coexisting correctly with the pre-existing 14 :market/* facts in the same conn. market-analyst grounding-gate verified end-to-end against real data: a mixed :gold-above-ground vs. Apple Inc. (CIK 0000320193) real-revenue comparison committed cleanly; a fabricated CIK forced a hard :grounding violation."
  :adr/cron-does-not-fire-mi-sec "IMPORTANT CAVEAT: .github/workflows/company-facts-refresh.yml was built (weekly cron + workflow_dispatch, auto-merge for data-only diffs per owner's confirmed preference) but GitHub Actions is disabled ORG-WIDE for gftdcojp (confirmed via gh api orgs/gftdcojp/actions/permissions -> {\"enabled\":false}). The workflow does not currently trigger. Establishing an actual periodic-execution mechanism (enabling gftdcojp Actions, or driving the refresh from this session's own scheduling infrastructure) is an explicit, unresolved follow-up -- not silently assumed to be working."
  :adr/test-status-mi-sec "market-intel: clojure -M:test 21 tests / 116 assertions, 0 failures, lint 0 errors. market-analyst: clojure -M:dev:test 18 tests / 64 assertions, 0 failures, lint 0 errors."
